Original commit body from ac967250faeba2c0060e18fcf8fa66b1490cab12:

One field name, two meanings: IoPrimitive.requires_target_kind holds a
TARGET KIND (std_stream), while TaintSource/TaintSink.requires_target_kind
held the BOUNDARY the call's target kind must resolve to, and
TaintSink.requires_mode held the boundary the mode argument selects.

The taint side is renamed: requires_target_kind -> requires_target_boundary
and requires_mode -> requires_mode_boundary, with their readers
(_target_kind_admits, the mode gate in _match_propagation_entry, the
derivation in _derive_auto_imports_from_io_primitives) and tests. The
catalogue row keeps requires_target_kind. No behaviour change; neither
field is serialised.

Addresses WI-dinop.

